<title>USA: TABLE-Cincinnati Bell Inc Q2 net rises.</title>
<headline>TABLE-Cincinnati Bell Inc Q2 net rises.</headline>
<dateline>CINCINNATI 1997-07-17</dateline>
<text>
<p>Quarter Ended June 30</p>
<p>					 1997	  1996    Change</p>
<p> Revenues			   $433.1    $376.0    $57.1  15%</p>
<p> Operating Income		   87.6(a)   74.5(b)  13.1  18%</p>
<p> Net Income			   54.2(a)   44.8(b)   9.4  21%</p>
<p> Earnings Per Common Share(1)   0.39(a)   0.32(b)   0.07 22%</p>
<p>Weighted Average Shares</p>
<p>Outstanding including</p>
<p>  equivalents (000)(1)	   137,604   137,892    (288)</p>
<p>				    Six Months Ended June 30</p>
<p>					 1997	  1996	  Change</p>
<p> Revenues			   $862.6   $ 738.1    $124.5  17%</p>
<p> Operating Income		  181.1(a)  147.1(b)   34.0  23%</p>
<p> Net Income			  111.4(a)   86.5(b)   24.9  29%</p>
<p> Earnings Per Common Share(1)   0.81(a)   0.63(b)   0.18  29%</p>
<p>Weighted Average Shares</p>
<p>Outstanding including</p>
<p>  equivalents (000)(1)	   137,566   137,044     522</p>
<p>In Millions, Except Per Share Amounts</p>
<p>NOTES (a) Special credits of $6.0 million for the second quarter and $21.0 million for the first six months are included in operating income. The credits increased net income $3.8 million or $0.02 per share for the second quarter and $13.4 million or $0.10 per share for the first six months.</p>
<p>(b) Special credits of $5.5 million for the second quarter and $11.0 million for the first six months are included in operating income. The credits increased net income $3.5 million or $0.02 per share for the second quarter and $7.0 million or $0.05 per share for the first six months.</p>
<p>(1) Restated to reflect two-for-one stock split in May 1997.</p>
<p>-- New York Newsdesk 212 859-1610</p>
